{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/15581-concordia-reimagined","id":15581,"title":"Concordia reimagined","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-21T13:26:11-08:00","id":15581,"title":"Concordia reimagined","content":"Does anyone have a list of the Changeling Kingdoms from Changeling the Dreaming? Or better yet an image of the map that showed the Kingdoms? I liked the idea of aligned freeholds so that if you want the option of anything beyond city level you could use it. This would make titles such as Duke and even King more poignant if some Kingdoms extended to multiple freeholds. I remember a thread discussing this very idea in the old forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T12:32:03-08:00","id":19309,"title":"","content":"You can get the maps on Google. Just search for &quot;Changeling Concordia map&quot; in image search.<br /> <br /> As far as using the actual Concordian kingdoms as a basis for a Lost North American setup...<br /> <br /> Pass.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's the thing. Most of the Kingdoms in Concordia ranged from boring to terrible. All of Canada is one massive frozen wasteland! All of the Midwest is a native paradise! Florida gets its own Kingdom for some reason because shut up! Mexico makes a weirdly specific Aztec joke which will never be explained! <br /> <br /> It was a weird mix of cultural stereotypes and arbitrary divisions that never really went anywhere. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Remember - popcorn can feel pain.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1195-frivyeti","name":"FrivYeti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T13:10:43-08:00","id":19328,"title":"","content":"Well I can't really find a good res image of the map through google, I never had the map really since my copy of the book was in PDF and they didn't include the map, unless that has changed with updates.<br /> <br /> Did they actually talk about them anywhere besides giving the names on the map? I thought they only detailed the Kingdom of Willows and the Kingdom of Apples in the books. Either way I like the idea of linking allied Freeholds under High Kings. I guess the issue is the Seasonal courts could mean you have a High King for each Court. Still in this setting not all freeholds would be linked in such a way, most would still be independent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T14:14:06-08:00","id":19895,"title":"","content":"The books you want for Concordian kingdoms are Nobles: the Shining Host, and War in Concordia. The former one discusses each kingdom and gives details about its ruler, and the latter discusses how the war affected them. There was also a lot about Pacifica in the Immortal Eyes. But I can't stress enough how dumb they are, so really, don't bother. (Also one Kingdom is ruled by a Duke, because shut up, that's why.)<br /> <br /> But yes, a general High King ruling over dozens of smaller kingdoms and serving as a mediator and such would be pretty cool.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Remember - popcorn can feel pain.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1195-frivyeti","name":"FrivYeti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}